Recently, sagernet blocked my account unilaterally and without any reason.
So this fork will not continue to provide support for new SB features in the future.
Goodbye. everyone.

For developers:
This is the sing-box 1.11 edition of luci-app-homeproxy.
Requires sing-box 1.11.x (tested with 1.11.1). It does NOT work with
sing-box 1.12.0 or later, and it is not an upgrade path for the 1.14 tree
in ../luci-app-homeproxy-master-1.14.4 - use that one for sing-box 1.14.x.

Generated sing-box configuration uses the legacy (1.11 compatible) format:
- DNS servers use the legacy `address` string format (`udp://`, `tcp://`,
  `tls://`, `https://`, `quic://`, `h3://`, `dhcp://`, `local`,
  `rcode://name_error`); the type based format is only available since 1.12.
- DNS rules use `action: "route"` + `server` (the `predefined`, `evaluate`
  and `match_response` actions only exist since 1.12/1.14). A `block-dns`
  server (`rcode://name_error`) provides the blocked answer.
- DNS response matching (`ip_cidr` / `ip_is_private`) was dropped by
  sing-box 1.11, so those DNS rule fields are not generated any more, and
  the DNS rule `outbound` field (a 1.14 domain resolver item) is ignored.
  Use the outbound/DNS server domain strategy options instead.
- A DNS rule that is left without any match condition is ignored (with a
  warning in the service log) instead of being written out: sing-box 1.11
  refuses to start with `parse dns rule[N]: missing conditions`. This
  affects the pre-seeded `nodes_domain` rule of the default configuration,
  which only carries an `outbound`; give it a domain or ruleset condition
  if it should match, otherwise it has no effect on 1.11.
- Outbound `domain_strategy` is used instead of `domain_resolver` and
  `route.default_domain_resolver` (both only exist since 1.14).
- TUN keeps `endpoint_independent_nat` instead of the 1.14 `udp_mapping` /
  `udp_filtering` fields.
- `experimental.cache_file.store_rdrc` is used instead of `store_dns`.
- Inline ACME is written to the `acme` TLS field instead of
  `certificate_provider`.
- wireguard (endpoint), rule actions (`sniff`, `hijack-dns`, `route`,
  `route-options`, `reject`) and the direct outbound `routing_mark` are
  already 1.11 features and are kept as is. Because the rule action
  `outbound` field accepts a single tag only, a routing rule with multiple
  outbounds is expanded into one rule per outbound.
- "Override destination" cannot be expressed by the `sniff` rule action on
  1.11: its `override_destination` field only exists since 1.12 and is
  rejected as an unknown field by 1.11. The deprecated inbound level fields
  (`sniff` / `sniff_override_destination`) are still honoured by 1.11, so they
  are written instead. In the custom routing mode sniffing is now always
  enabled and the switch only controls the destination override: an
  unsniffed connection carries no domain, so every domain/ruleset condition
  of the custom rules stops matching and the traffic is silently handed to
  the default outbound, which looks like "no internet" whenever that outbound
  is not a proxy. Clearing the switch keeps the domain based routing and only
  leaves the destination address untouched (the outbound receives the ip).
  Only the custom routing mode reads the switch from the configuration (the
  other modes have always forced global sniffing), so the behaviour of
  bypass/gfwlist/tun is unchanged.
- A selector never carries a `default` outbound which is not part of its own
  outbound list, and a urltest never carries a `default` at all: sing-box
  1.11 refuses both. When the configured default node is gone (removed by a
  subscription update), filtered out, or not a member of the selected
  subscription groups, the first outbound is used and a warning is logged.
  The default outbound dropdown of a group based selector lists the nodes of
  the selected subscription groups.

Firewall:
- Port 53 is no longer part of the default "common ports" list. DNS is
  served by dnsmasq and the sing-box DNS inbound, transparently proxying
  UDP/53 broke name resolution for the whole LAN in custom routing mode.
  The nft rules also always return UDP/53 in the tproxy and tun paths, so
  existing configurations which still list port 53 keep working.

Upgrading:
- LuCI serves the view JavaScript files from /www/luci-static/resources with
  long lived caching, and the URL is not versioned. After installing a new
  package, hard refresh the browser (Ctrl/Cmd + Shift + R, or clear the site
  cache) before judging the UI. Otherwise the old node.js keeps running and
  newly added fields (for example the "Default Outbound" row of a selector)
  appear to be missing even though the installed file is correct.

